\description{
Turn per-crop harvested-derived physical area into a fallow-inclusive physical
land extension whose arable-crop total reconciles to FAO's physical
\strong{Arable land} and whose perennial-crop total reconciles to FAO's physical
\strong{Permanent crops} (\code{\link[=get_arable_permanent_land]{get_arable_permanent_land()}}), per \verb{(area_code, year)}.

This is the FAO-land-base analogue of \code{\link[=build_cropgrids_land_extension]{build_cropgrids_land_extension()}}\code{(source = "cropgrids_fallow")}. The existing method takes the fallow \emph{magnitude} from
FAOSTAT "Temporary fallow" (item 6640, a sparse and, for many rain-fed
economies, absent series) applied to a single CROPGRIDS 2020 snapshot. Here
the fallow magnitude is the physical arable land that carried no harvest in
that specific year, \verb{FAO Arable land - sum(cropped arable physical)}, so a
drought year's resting cropland is charged to the crops whose rotation it
supports and the arable-crop footprint totals match FAO's land survey in every
year (see the Tunisia/Portugal motivation in \code{\link[=get_arable_permanent_land]{get_arable_permanent_land()}}).

